# Danlite ELM ADMIN portal — environment template
#
# Copy to .env.local and fill in there. .env.local is gitignored and must
# never be committed. This template holds NAMES ONLY.
#
# ── WHAT IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT ────────────────────────────────────────
# There is NO SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY here, and there must never be one.
#
# This app renders every customer's data, but it does so by ASKING the admin
# Edge Functions for it over HTTPS, carrying the signed-in admin's own JWT.
# The functions hold service_role; this app does not. That is the whole
# security story of the admin portal in one line:
#
#     compromising this Next.js app gets you a session, not the database.
#
# If a future change ever seems to need the service key here, the correct fix
# is a new read-only Edge Function, not a new line in this file.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
